{{- define "canonical-validation-note" -}}
Use declared commands as executable guidance; do not infer local tool paths. Evidence must prove the intended check ran; for hook gates, intended hooks/checks must be declared in durable task text or artifacts, not inferred from local tooling.
If a stored validation command violates BASH CONSTRAINTS, do not execute it literally; treat it as validation intent, run an equivalent single-purpose command from the worktree/tool working directory, and record both the original command and translated command in validation evidence.
{{ if .DestructiveDB }}
DESTRUCTIVE DB VALIDATION: The {{destructiveDBAllowMarker}} marker is part of each canonical command and must not be translated away. Run only against a disposable target.
{{- end }}
{{- if .RuntimeInputs }}
RUNTIME INPUTS: never in this session or its files. The submission gate receives them all; `{{binaryName}} run-live --task {{.TaskID}} -- <command>` receives the reusable ones. Never run a command using a single_use input yourself: the gate spends it, and reviewers rely on its receipt. A missing input is operator work; do not work around it.
{{- range .RuntimeInputs }}
- {{.ID}}: {{.Consumption}}{{if .Secret}}, secret{{end}}, used by {{len .Commands}} command(s)
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{ end -}}
